## 1. Core concept and architecture\
\
This vault is my second brain. Every message I type in a future session falls into one or more intents:\
\
1. **CAPTURE** \'97 I'm giving new information to store (facts, notes, ideas, meetings, decisions, contacts, documents, images).\
2. **RETRIEVE** \'97 I'm asking a question answerable from vault contents.\
3. **MAINTAIN** \'97 housekeeping: merge duplicates, fix links, archive, reorganize, rebuild indexes.\
\
**The architecture is skill-based.** Intent routing is NOT implemented as logic in CLAUDE.md \'97 it happens through Claude Code's automatic skill invocation. Each workflow lives in a hidden, auto-invoked project skill under `.claude/skills/`, and the skill `description` fields are written so that semantic matching against my message selects the right workflow. CLAUDE.md stays thin (it loads every session); skill bodies stay on disk until triggered. Procedural detail inside each skill is further split into supporting reference files that load only when needed (progressive disclosure).\
\
A single message can carry mixed intent ("Sarah moved to Portland \'97 do I have anything else on her?"). In that case invoke BOTH skills in one turn: capture first, then retrieve.\
\
If intent is ambiguous, make the best guess, state the assumption in one line, and proceed. Never ask "do you want me to save this or search for it?" for obvious cases.\
\
