## 4. Skill 1: capture-workflow (hidden, auto-invoked)\
\
`.claude/skills/capture-workflow/SKILL.md`\
\
**Frontmatter:** `user-invocable: false`. Do NOT set `disable-model-invocation`.\
\
**Description (write it for reliable triggering, contrastive with retrieval):** something like \'97 "Use whenever the user provides information to store: declarative statements of fact, 'note that', 'remember this', 'save this', 'add to', pasted content, dropped files/images/PDFs, meeting summaries, or corrections to stored info ('actually it's X not Y'). Covers filing, note creation/editing, linking, reorganization, and attachments. Do NOT use for questions about existing information \'97 that is retrieval-format."\
\
**SKILL.md body \'97 a tight checklist, not an essay:**\
1. Classify the content type (fact, project update, person, meeting, journal entry, document, idea, preference, task/deadline).\
2. Preference about answer style? \uc0\u8594  edit `_system/preferences.md`, confirm in one line, done.\
3. Search the vault FIRST for an existing home (grep title keywords + synonyms, check `_system/index.md` and the relevant MOC). Prefer appending/updating over creating.\
4. If creating: pick destination folder (read its CLAUDE.md), use the matching `_templates/` template, fill frontmatter per `_system/conventions.md`.\
5. **Stamp real dates everywhere.** Use the actual current date (run `date` if unsure \'97 never guess) for `created`/`updated` frontmatter and for any dated content. Resolve relative dates I use ("next Friday", "in two weeks", "last month") into absolute YYYY-MM-DD dates in the note, keeping my phrasing if useful ("follow up next Friday (2026-07-17)").\
6. **Anything with a due/expiry/follow-up date is a task, not just a fact.** Record it in the relevant note as an Obsidian checkbox with a date: `- [ ] Renew passport \uc0\u55357 \u56517  2027-03-01`. Also add a matching line to `Upcoming.md` under the right month, linking back to the source note. When I say something is done, check the box in the source note and remove it from Upcoming.md.\
7. **Person/entity notes get an `aliases` frontmatter list** \'97 every name variant, nickname, email, or handle they might be referenced by (e.g., `aliases: [Sarah, Sarah Chen, sarah@acme.com]`). Add new aliases as they appear in later captures.\
8. Weave links: add `[[wikilinks]]` to every related existing note; add backlinks in those notes where natural; update the area MOC; update Home.md only if a new major area appeared.\
9. **Update `_system/index.md`**: add a line for every new note (title | type | tags | updated date); update the line on renames/moves.\
10. Attachment involved? \uc0\u8594  follow `attachments.md` in this skill folder.\
11. Note grew past ~300 lines, duplicates found, or content is misfiled? \uc0\u8594  follow `reorganization.md`.\
12. Unclear where it belongs? \uc0\u8594  file in `00-Inbox/` with a one-line "needs filing" marker.\
13. Confirm to the user in 1\'962 lines: what was stored, where, what was linked.\
\
**Supporting file `attachments.md`:** copy binary into `_attachments/` named `YYYY-MM-DD-description.ext`; create/update a companion note in the right folder that embeds the file (`![[...]]`), summarizes its contents as searchable text (read the PDF / describe the image), and lists the path under an `attachments:` frontmatter key.\
\
**Supporting file `reorganization.md`:** criteria and procedures for splitting oversized notes into linked sub-notes, merging duplicates, moving misfiled notes, and archiving; the mandatory link-refactor rule \'97 on any move/rename, grep the entire vault for wikilinks and markdown links to the old name/path and update every reference; changelog logging format.\
