## 7. _system files and templates\
\
**conventions.md** \'97 single source of truth:\
- Frontmatter schema required on every note:\
  ```yaml\
  ---\
  created: YYYY-MM-DD\
  updated: YYYY-MM-DD\
  type: note | project | person | meeting | journal | reference | attachment-note\
  tags: []\
  aliases: [] (person/entity notes: all name variants, nicknames, emails, handles)\
  status: (projects only)\
  attachments: [] (only if any)\
  ---\
  ```\
  `updated` must be bumped on every edit. All dates are real calendar dates \'97 resolve relative phrasing to absolute YYYY-MM-DD at capture time.\
- Task format: `- [ ] description \uc0\u55357 \u56517  YYYY-MM-DD` for anything with a due/expiry/follow-up date; tasks live in their topical note AND get a linked line in `Upcoming.md`.\
- Naming: notes in Title Case; journal and meeting notes date-prefixed; attachments date-prefixed kebab-case.\
- Tagging: small controlled vocabulary, lowercase, hyphenated; prefer links over tags; list a starter tag set.\
- Linking: minimum one wikilink per note; MOCs link down, notes link laterally.\
\
**preferences.md** \'97 my answer-style preferences, structured so individual rules are easy to edit. Starting defaults:\
- Default style: short summary first (2\'964 sentences), details only if asked.\
- Bullets only when listing 3+ discrete facts; otherwise prose.\
- Verbosity triggers: go detailed when the question says "everything", "in detail", "full history", or similar.\
- Always end with wikilinked sources.\
- Per-topic overrides: an initially-empty section where topic-specific preferences accumulate (e.g., "finance questions: always include dates and amounts").\
\
**changelog.md** \'97 header row explaining the one-line-per-change format.\
\
**index.md** \'97 the retrieval shortlist: one line per note in the format `title | type | tags | updated`. Initialize it with all seed notes; capture keeps it current; maintenance rebuilds it from scratch.\
\
**Upcoming.md** (vault root) \'97 the rolling deadlines view: sections per month, each line an unchecked task with its \uc0\u55357 \u56517  date and a wikilink to the source note, overdue items flagged at top. Initialize empty with the section structure and a one-line explanation.\
\
**_staging/** \'97 add a short README explaining: "Drop exports here (Apple Notes, docs, old vault files). Then ask Claude to 'import my staging folder' \'97 files get processed into proper notes and originals are archived."\
\
**_templates/** \'97 create `note.md`, `project.md`, `person.md`, `meeting.md`, `daily.md`, `attachment-note.md`, each with frontmatter and section stubs.\
