## 10. Onboarding interview (run AFTER the structure is built)\
\
Once every folder, file, and skill from sections 2\'969 exists, switch modes and interview me. This is the only part of the whole setup where you SHOULD ask me questions.\
\
**How to run it:**\
- Ask in small batches (2\'964 questions at a time), conversationally, not as one giant form. Wait for my answers before the next batch.\
- Every answer is a capture: file it into the vault following the capture-workflow rules (real notes, proper frontmatter, wikilinks, MOC updates) \'97 not a single dump file.\
- I can skip any question or say "done" to end the interview early. Skipped topics are simply left out.\
\
**Cover at minimum:**\
1. **Identity basics** \'97 name, what I do, where I'm based. \uc0\u8594  a "Me" note at the vault root or in `20-Personal/`, linked from Home.md.\
2. **Work landscape** \'97 my job/business, active projects, key people I work with, tools/companies I deal with regularly. \uc0\u8594  seed notes in `10-Work/Projects/` and `10-Work/People/`.\
3. **Personal landscape** \'97 family members and important people, health topics I track, financial areas I want organized, home/vehicle basics. \uc0\u8594  seed notes in `20-Personal/` subfolders.\
4. **Interests and knowledge areas** \'97 topics I read about, hobbies, things I want to build knowledge on. \uc0\u8594  stub notes in `30-Knowledge/` linked to the Knowledge MOC.\
5. **Habits and preferences** \'97 how I like answers formatted (update `_system/preferences.md` with anything I say), whether I plan to journal daily, anything I explicitly do NOT want stored.\
\
**After the interview:** review what was created and reorganize if needed \'97 if my answers revealed that the default folder structure doesn't fit my life (e.g., I have two businesses, or no use for a Travel folder), rename/add/remove folders accordingly, update the affected CLAUDE.md files and MOCs, fix all links, and log the changes in the changelog. The structure should end up shaped around MY life, not the template.\
