## 11. Usage guide (print this at the very end)\
\
After the interview and reorganization, print a short "How to use your Second Brain" guide directly in the chat, AND save it as `How To Use This Vault.md` at the vault root (linked from Home.md) so I can reread it in Obsidian. It must explain, with concrete examples:\
\
**Adding information \'97 just state it.** No command needed; declarative statements route to capture automatically:\
- "Sarah from Acme is now my main contact for the Q3 project, her email is sarah@acme.com"\
- "Note that my car insurance renews March 15, policy #ABC123"\
- "Here's the contract PDF from the vendor" (with a dropped file)\
- "Actually, the meeting got moved to Thursday" (corrections update existing notes)\
\
**Retrieving \'97 just ask.** Questions route to retrieval automatically:\
- "What do I know about Sarah from Acme?"\
- "When does my car insurance renew?"\
- "Summarize everything about the Q3 project"\
- "Do I have anything on vendor contracts from last year?"\
- Time-based questions work too: "What did I decide last month?" / "What's coming up in the next two weeks?" / "What's overdue?"\
\
**Deadlines and follow-ups \'97 state them like anything else.** Anything with a date becomes a tracked task automatically:\
- "My passport expires March 2027" \uc0\u8594  checkbox task in the passport note + a line in [[Upcoming]]\
- "Follow up with Wade next week" \uc0\u8594  resolved to a real date and tracked\
- "I renewed the passport" \uc0\u8594  the task gets checked off and leaves Upcoming\
\
**Importing existing notes \'97 use the staging folder.** Export from Apple Notes, Google Docs, old vaults, etc., drop the files into `_staging/`, then say "import my staging folder". Files are split into proper notes, filed, linked, and the originals archived. Do this in batches if you have a lot.\
\
**Capturing from your phone.** Sync this folder (iCloud, Obsidian Sync, or git) and open it in Obsidian mobile. Jot quick notes into `00-Inbox/` from anywhere \'97 no special format needed. Next time you're in Claude Code, say "clean up my inbox" and everything gets filed properly.\
\
**Changing how answers look \'97 just say so.** These edit preferences and stick permanently:\
- "Keep answers shorter" / "Always use bullet points" / "For finance questions, always include dates and amounts"\
\
**Maintenance \'97 ask or run the command:**\
- "Clean up my inbox" / "Do a weekly review" / "Find broken links" \'97 or type `/vault-maintenance`\
\
**Tips section:** mixed messages work (store + ask in one sentence); when unsure where something went, ask "where did you file that?"; open the folder in Obsidian anytime \'97 the graph view shows how notes connect; nothing is ever deleted, only archived.\
